---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {tools} from '../../config';
---
<Base title="Free Financial Calculators" path="/tools/" description="Free compound interest, monthly investment, loan payment and savings goal calculators. Private browser-based tools with clear assumptions.">
<div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Tools</div><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Tools / Free calculators</span><h1>Clarity starts with the numbers.</h1><p>Explore possible outcomes before making financial decisions. These four calculators work in your browser—there's no account, upload or personal data collection.</p></header>
<section class="section archive-section" aria-label="Finance calculators"><div class="archive-heading"><span>04 free calculators</span><span>Illustrative estimates, not forecasts</span></div><div class="tool-grid">{tools.map((tool,index)=><a href={`/tools/${tool.slug}/`} class="tool-card"><span class="tool-symbol" aria-hidden="true">0{index+1} /</span><h3>{tool.name}</h3><p>{tool.description}</p><span class="tool-link">Open calculator ↗</span></a>)}</div></section>
<div class="calculator-guide"><h2>What these estimates do—and don't—tell you</h2><p>Each calculator uses a fixed-rate mathematical model. It helps show how changing an assumption affects the result, but cannot predict returns, product costs, inflation, taxes, losses or personal eligibility. Review the explanation on each calculator page before acting on its numbers.</p><p>For context on long-term compounding, start with <a class="text-link" href="/articles/compound-interest-explained/">our compound interest guide</a>.</p></div></div>
</Base>
